// The iOS half of the telemetry configuration (spec §18.7).
//
//     cp ios/Telemetry.xcconfig.example ios/Telemetry.xcconfig
//
// `ios/Telemetry.xcconfig` is **untracked and required to exist** — `xcodegen generate` fails and
// names it when it does not, which is the loud failure a missing endpoint is supposed to be. Copied
// as it stands, with both values empty, **the client is inert**: nothing is queued and nothing is
// sent (conventions.md, Configuration — no endpoint is ever defaulted in code). Fill both in to
// turn it on; `ios/project.yml` substitutes them into the generated Info.plist, which is where
// `Telemetry.swift` reads them.
//
// ⚠️ `//` starts a comment in an xcconfig, so a pasted `https://…` silently truncates to `https:`
// and the endpoint quietly becomes nonsense. Write the URL host-first after `$(SMASH_SCHEME)`,
// which reassembles the scheme through an empty `$()` expansion — that is what keeps the two
// slashes apart in the file:
SMASH_SCHEME = https:/$()/

// The collector (spec §18.6): $(SMASH_SCHEME)ingest.nann.in/smash
SMASH_TELEMETRY_URL   =

// On the box: `grep SH_INGEST_TOKEN /opt/smashhockey/.env`. Not a secret in any real sense — it
// ships inside the binary — but it never belongs in a commit, a ticket or a chat.
SMASH_TELEMETRY_TOKEN =
